---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects | Aaron Kyle Villegas" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Featured Projects</div>
  </div>

  <!-- 1. Walmart Retail Sales & Inventory Strategy Analysis -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Walmart Retail Sales & Inventory Strategy Analysis"
    img="/walmart-analytics.webp"
    desc="Retail demand analysis across 45 stores and 2 years of weekly sales data. Modeled holiday seasonality (including a 69% Christmas surge) and store-level demand variance using Coefficient of Variation (CV) to spot where safety stock ran thin. Built a Tableau dashboard comparing year-over-year revenue, store tiers, and 30-day rolling sales."
    url="/blog/walmart-sales"
    badge="Retail Analytics"
    tags={["Python", "SQL", "Tableau", "Pandas", "Demand Planning"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read Case Study", url: "/blog/walmart-sales", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "Tableau Dashboard", url: "https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/aaron.villegas3123/viz/WalmartSalesAnalysis_17802549747750/KPIDashboard", target: "_blank" },
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/walmart_data_analysis", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 2. Multi-Echelon Replenishment & Stockout Risk Simulator -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Multi-Echelon Replenishment & Stockout Risk Simulator"
    desc="Interactive supply chain simulator that models safety stock, reorder points, and lead-time variability across 50,000+ orders. Uses DuckDB for sub-second local SQL queries without database overhead, SciPy Monte Carlo simulations to calculate stockout risks under demand spikes, and Streamlit/Plotly for scenario testing."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/supply-chain-replenishment-simulator"
    badge="Inventory Analytics"
    tags={["Python", "DuckDB", "SciPy", "Streamlit", "Plotly", "Monte Carlo"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/supply-chain-replenishment-simulator", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 3. Macroeconomic & Climate Analytics Platform (Macro Data Pipeline) -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Macroeconomic & Climate Analytics Platform (Macro Data Pipeline)"
    img="/macro-pipeline.webp"
    desc="Data platform that ingests 9M+ time-series records from FRED, Open-Meteo, and US Census Retail APIs into PostgreSQL and BigQuery. Orchestrated daily with Apache Airflow in Docker and modeled in BigQuery with dbt. Features a SARIMAX forecasting engine for retail trends and a FastAPI backend with a Gemini agent that answers plain-English questions using four BigQuery query tools."
    url="/blog/macro-data-pipeline"
    badge="Data Engineering"
    tags={["Python", "Apache Airflow", "dbt", "BigQuery", "Snowflake", "PostgreSQL", "Docker", "FastAPI", "SARIMAX"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read Case Study", url: "/blog/macro-data-pipeline", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/macro-data-pipeline", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 4. The Frontier Brief -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="The Frontier Brief: Daily AI Intelligence Pipeline"
    desc="A daily AI briefing I built and run. Every morning it pulls from AI lab blogs, Reddit, Hacker News, Mastodon and GitHub Trending, ranks what matters, and drafts the newsletter with a writer model. A second model reviews the draft, and plain code checks catch repeated wording and mismatched names before it goes out. Each edition is emailed through Buttondown and saved to a public archive. It runs on GitHub Actions for about 30 cents a day, retries on failure, alerts me if a day is missed, and has 440+ tests."
    url="https://aaronvillegas5.github.io/frontier-brief/"
    badge="Autonomous Pipeline"
    tags={["Python", "OpenAI API", "GitHub Actions", "Buttondown", "Supabase", "pytest"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read the Latest Edition", url: "https://aaronvillegas5.github.io/frontier-brief/", target: "_blank", primary: true }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 5. Home Server on a Raspberry Pi 5 -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Home Server on a Raspberry Pi 5"
    desc="A headless Raspberry Pi 5 I set up and run at home. It runs background Python jobs and AI workflows, checks an inbox over IMAP for job-application emails, takes deduplicated backups with Rustic, and keeps files in sync across my machines with Syncthing."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5"
    badge="Edge Systems"
    tags={["ARM64 Linux", "Docker", "Python", "Node.js", "IMAP/TLS", "Rustic", "Syncthing", "ZRAM"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 6. Environmental Health Risk Mapping Platform -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Environmental Health Risk Mapping Platform"
    img="/env-risk-map.webp"
    desc="Won Best Visualization out of 39 teams. Blended CalEnviroScreen, EPA, and census data covering 8,000+ California census tracts into a composite Health Vulnerability Index. Trained XGBoost models to predict respiratory and cardiac risk factors, deployed behind a FastAPI service for real-time risk scores and nearest-neighbor lookups."
    url="/blog/environmental-health-risk-map"
    badge="Datathon Winner"
    tags={["Python", "XGBoost", "FastAPI", "Spatial Analysis", "Machine Learning"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read Case Study", url: "/blog/environmental-health-risk-map", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "Live Demo", url: "https://environmental-health-risk-map.vercel.app", target: "_blank" },
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/environmental-health-risk-map", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 7. ResuMatch: AI Resume & Job Description Analyzer -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="ResuMatch: AI Resume & Job Description Analyzer"
    desc="Resume analysis tool built during ZotHacks. Uses Python, FastAPI, and OpenAI to parse resumes against job postings, running TF-IDF keyword extraction and text matching to highlight missing qualifications."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5"
    badge="ZotHacks Hackathon"
    tags={["Python", "FastAPI", "OpenAI API", "React", "NLP", "TF-IDF"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 8. A/B Testing Analysis -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="A/B Testing Analysis of Digital Marketing Campaigns"
    img="/ab-testing.webp"
    desc="Statistical hypothesis testing on 588,000+ customer records. Used unequal-group power analysis and two-proportion z-tests to measure conversion differences, validating a statistically significant 0.76 percentage-point conversion lift (1.79% to 2.55%, p < 0.001) to guide advertising spend."
    url="/blog/ab-test-marketing-campaign"
    badge="A/B Testing"
    tags={["Python", "statsmodels", "A/B Testing", "Hypothesis Testing", "Pandas", "Seaborn"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read Case Study", url: "/blog/ab-test-marketing-campaign", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/ABTest-MarketingCampaign", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 9. Predicting Marketing Success with Machine Learning -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Predicting Marketing Success with Machine Learning"
    img="/marketing-ml.webp"
    desc="Customer targeting model trained on 40,000+ bank marketing records. Addressed class imbalance using SMOTE and threshold tuning (85% accuracy, 0.62 recall), evaluating random forest feature importance to identify which macroeconomic indicators correlated most with deposit subscriptions."
    url="/blog/bank-marketing-ml"
    badge="Machine Learning"
    tags={["Python", "scikit-learn", "Pandas", "SQL", "SMOTE", "Random Forest"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Read Case Study", url: "/blog/bank-marketing-ml", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5/uci-bank-marketing-analysis", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 10. Global Superstore Data Normalization & Analytics Dashboard -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Global Superstore Data Normalization & Analytics Dashboard"
    desc="Normalized a flat dataset of 51,290 global sales records into a 3-table relational schema (Orders Fact, Customers Dim, Products Dim) with primary and foreign keys to eliminate duplication. Built Excel Pivot Table dashboards tracking regional profitability and shipping fulfillment lead times."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5"
    badge="BI & Modeling"
    tags={["Excel", "Data Normalization", "Pivot Tables", "XLOOKUP", "Relational Modeling"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 11. Fixed-Income & Portfolio Modeling -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Fixed-Income & Portfolio Modeling"
    img="/portfolio-modeling.webp"
    desc="Excel financial models applying Markowitz portfolio theory and the one-fund theorem to calculate efficient asset allocations. Evaluated bond pricing, cash flow schedules, and yield to maturity, modeling duration matching and portfolio immunization techniques."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5"
    badge="Quant Modeling"
    tags={["Excel", "Portfolio Theory", "Fixed Income", "Risk Management"]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 12. Numerical Linear Algebra & Algorithmic Stability -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Numerical Linear Algebra & Algorithmic Stability"
    desc="UCI Directed Reading Program project in computational math. Implemented Classical vs. Modified Gram-Schmidt and QR decomposition in Python to benchmark loss of orthogonality on ill-conditioned Hilbert matrices. Built an SVD algorithm from scratch using iterative QR decomposition on A^TA for image rank approximations."
    url="https://github.com/AaronVillegas5"
    badge="Computational Math"
    tags={["Python", "NumPy", "OpenCV", "Matplotlib", "SVD", "LaTeX"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "GitHub", url: "https://github.com/AaronVillegas5", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>

  <!-- 13. Black-Scholes Model Paper -->
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Deriving & Understanding the Black-Scholes Option Pricing Model"
    img="/black-scholes.webp"
    desc="Research paper deriving the Black-Scholes PDE using Ito's Lemma, Geometric Brownian Motion, and dynamic delta hedging under no-arbitrage assumptions. Reviews risk-neutral valuation, martingale pricing, and limitations when volatility is stochastic."
    url="/projects/black-scholes-paper"
    target="_self"
    badge="Research Paper"
    tags={["Quantitative Finance", "Stochastic Calculus", "LaTeX", "Option Pricing"]}
    custom_links={[
      { text: "Preview Paper", url: "/projects/black-scholes-paper", target: "_self", primary: true },
      { text: "Download PDF", url: "/black-scholes-paper.pdf", target: "_blank" }
    ]}
  />
</BaseLayout>